00:27:42.745 --> 00:27:46.615
And this gets me to my why
this matters moment for today.

00:27:46.715 --> 00:27:47.883
Why does this matter?

00:27:47.983 --> 00:27:50.853
Why does counting and thinking
about how much of stuff

00:27:50.953 --> 00:27:55.057
you're using by using
chemistry and moles?

00:27:55.157 --> 00:27:55.924
Why does that matter?

00:27:56.025 --> 00:27:58.661
Well, let's take an example.

00:27:58.761 --> 00:28:02.131
Let's take an example of
nothing less than the number

00:28:02.231 --> 00:28:04.700
of humans on this planet.

00:28:04.800 --> 00:28:07.169
This is the
population of humans.

00:28:07.269 --> 00:28:12.307
And you can see that it wasn't
all that much until lately.

00:28:12.408 --> 00:28:14.810
But let's focus in
on this part here.

00:28:14.910 --> 00:28:16.245
Let's focus in on
that part there.

00:28:16.345 --> 00:28:17.079
Right.

00:28:17.179 --> 00:28:18.247
So that's billions of people.

00:28:18.347 --> 00:28:21.517
So if I zoom in on
